#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105436 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105858 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9e4943a-72d7-545e-b746-3a19ee6d3a83" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Segments and Their Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "a9ca2de5-c0ad-5bba-a432-0e62fdcd7d9c" :question/math-academy-id "e-10583" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8e1231cbb099e15fe3b7e334cdf3abff1550a8903b2f641be579d2b5ee1de770.png)\n\nWhat is the correct way to represent the line segment shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Since the segment has endpoints $R$ and $Q,$ we can represent this line segment as follows:\n\n$$\n\\overline{RQ}\n$$\n\nWe draw a horizontal line $(\\overline{\\phantom{\\_\\_}})$ with no arrows above our letters to denote that the line does not extend forever."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105437 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105859 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f50316d-ff00-53a1-af3a-fedd68e91f43" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rays and Their Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "acae6ded-25d0-5ed3-bd39-8c81ecd9a4d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-10603" :question/problem "![](images/3e/3e5984eebce9ba2600c980df7910ec2e92b351ea9ae29e8ad30209814deca2dd.png)\n\nConsider the points $R$ and $S$ shown above. Draw the ray $\\overset{\\longrightarrow}{RS}.$" :question/worked-solution "Note the following:\n\n- A ray is a straight object with a specific starting point and extends forever in **one** direction.\n\n- Using diagrams, a ray is shown with an arrow on **one** side.\n\nIn our case, the starting point is $R,$ and the ray extends in the $S$ direction. Therefore, we can draw the ray as follows: \n\n![](images/43/43aaca7cab8f55253aa781896e2ca0070faf6a3c98b98af3950ed307f82f7898.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105520 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8db8b0ae-1a2a-546a-884d-bdf773c75483" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Lines and Their Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "569e004c-b3c0-5389-9942-fd6dbcad046e" :question/math-academy-id "e-2540" :question/problem "What is the correct way to represent the line shown below?\n\n![](images/ea/ea118ccb0db48300f671461a5617d1bb7d1679454e083adab43e4fc2d9bc36f0.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since the line passes through the points $S$ and $T,$ we can represent this line as follows:\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\longleftrightarrow}{ST}\n$$\n\nWe use the \"$\\longleftrightarrow$\" symbol to denote that the line extends forever in **both** directions."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105859 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f50316d-ff00-53a1-af3a-fedd68e91f43" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Rays and Their Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60a8ad14-a2a4-589b-81b8-e401b50746ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{⟶}{XY}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430228} {:answer/id #uuid "7f549313-f67e-5a4d-9cd0-90aef3de787c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{⟷}{XY}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430234} {:answer/id #uuid "833f27dc-aa6a-5612-a780-c56a53b8b524" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "XY" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430235} {:answer/id #uuid "a8da28fe-814a-5311-9efb-3a3e37b437cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{⟵}{XY}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430239} {:answer/id #uuid "d95c4615-f26d-5bbd-8d6d-70bc48b3d889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{―}{XY}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60a8ad14-a2a4-589b-81b8-e401b50746ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{⟶}{XY}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430228} :answer-field